// wrangler.jsonc: lets Cloudflare build and serve the browser demo (ADR-93) from this repository: a Worker that is
// static assets only, the site the `web` build makes (build-web/site). Nothing in the project's own build or CI reads
// this file; CI publishes the same site to GitHub Pages by itself (.github/workflows/ci.yml, `publish`).
//
// In the Cloudflare dashboard (Workers & Pages, import a repository), the Worker must be named as `name` below, and:
//
//   Build command    bash Scripts/cloudflare-build.sh
//                    (name bash: the builder was seen to run a build command in plain sh, where Emscripten's
//                    environment script cannot find itself; Cloudflare's documentation names no shell. The script
//                    installs CMake and Ninja with pip and Emscripten at the version cmake/FcmpDeps.cmake pins,
//                    outside the checkout, and builds the site alone.)
//   Deploy command   npx wrangler deploy   (the default)
//   Preview builds   off (Settings, Build, Branch control): only `main` is built and served. The user's decision,
//                    2026-10-03: a pull request's branch is work in progress, and CI's gate has not seen it.
//
// Cloudflare compiles its own copy: what it serves is this commit's site, but not the artifact CI's browser gate
// tested (that one is what GitHub Pages serves).
{
  "name": "fcompressor",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-03",
  // Served at the user's own domain, https://fcompressor.seanfunk.xyz, and at the Worker's workers.dev address,
  // https://fcompressor.seantfunk.workers.dev. The domain is attached in the Cloudflare dashboard (the user said so
  // on 2026-10-05), not here: this file lists no `routes`, and wrangler publishes custom domains and routes only
  // when the configuration lists some (read in `triggersDeploy` in the source of wrangler 4.100.0 and of 4.147.0,
  // the version Cloudflare's builder ran on its earlier deploys). So a deploy leaves the domain as it is.
  // `preview_urls` false gives an uploaded version no address of its own (a Version URL) and a Preview of another
  // branch none either. `workers_dev` and `preview_urls` are both stated so that a deploy does not have to warn about
  // a default.
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./build-web/site"
  }
}
